AUTHORSHIP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Handrail is an original product designed and built by Maaz Kazi.

The product itself — what Handrail is, who it is for, how it behaves, and every
part of how it works — is original work:

  - the product concept and its positioning (PRODUCT.md)
  - the guided-task model: plan, point, watch, correct
  - the on-screen pointing system, its geometry, and the arrow's visual rules
    (src/main/geometry.js, renderer/arrow.js)
  - the step-watching loop and its cost model
    (src/main/turn.js, and PRODUCT.md § Step completion)
  - the entire prompt layer (src/main/prompts.js)
  - the entire main process (src/main/)
  - the entire renderer: overlay, arrow and onboarding (renderer/)
  - the IPC contract (preload.js, preload-arrow.js, docs/IPC.md)
  - the OpenRouter provider adapter (src/services/openrouter.adapter.js)
  - the brand, identity and design system (design/)
  - the build, packaging and release tooling (scripts/, .github/workflows/)
  - all documentation (README.md, PRODUCT.md, DECISIONS.md, CONTEXT.md,
    PLATFORM.md, DEPLOYMENT.md, docs/)

Every file listed above carries a copyright header naming its author. The
authorship record is also in the git history: commit 7909792 is the pristine
upstream import and nothing else, so `git diff 7909792..HEAD` is exactly and
only the original work.

